// Main Prisma schema file — generator and datasource blocks ONLY.
//
// This project uses Prisma's multi-file schema support (GA since v6.7.0).
// Domain models live under `prisma/models/*.prisma`, one file per
// `src/modules/*` business module, mirroring the accepted bounded-context
// ownership recorded in `docs/domain/domain-model.md` and ADR 0001-0011.
//
// Physical design translation only — see `prisma/models/README.md` and the
// PR/ADR that approved this schema for the full mapping rationale. No
// architecture, ERD, or entity-boundary decision is made in this file or its
// sibling model files; every table, relationship, and constraint here is a
// direct, faithful translation of already-accepted documentation.

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

// NOTE (Prisma ORM v7): the datasource `url` is configured in
// `prisma.config.ts`, not here — schema-level `url` is no longer supported.
//
// `schemas` enables PostgreSQL multi-schema support (GA since Prisma 6.13,
// no `previewFeatures` flag required). Every Postgres schema below maps
// 1:1 to one `src/modules/*` bounded context. Cross-schema relations are
// ordinary Postgres foreign keys — Prisma imposes no extra ceremony beyond
// declaring the target schema in this list and tagging each model with
// `@@schema(...)`.
//
// NOTE: the Prisma parser in this version requires the `schemas` array to
// be a single line within the `datasource` block (a multi-line array here
// fails validation with "not a valid definition within a datasource").
// Modules, in order: CRM Core (organization schema = single-company
// substrate; users, rbac, customers, leads, follow_ups, campaigns), Loan
// Management, Telephony, Documents, Notifications, Reports, and the AI
// Platform's six sibling schemas. There is no multi-organization product
// surface — `organizationId` is company-scope only.
datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  schemas  = ["organization", "users", "rbac", "customers", "leads", "follow_ups", "campaigns", "lead_center", "integrations", "banks", "loan_products", "loan_applications", "loan_accounts", "disbursements", "telephony", "documents", "notifications", "reports", "ai_core", "ai_documents", "ai_telephony", "ai_crm", "ai_analytics", "ai_governance"]
}
